    "created_at": "2018-07-09T14:30:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-07-09T14:30:45Z",
    "body": "What is being asked - For WebKit to stop using the title in back/forward list entries because other browsers don’t?\r\n\r\nSince it’s advisory, what’s wrong with that status quo?\r\n\r\nWe were *never* going to allow JavaScript to dynamically script the title displayed in the current browser tab in such an obvious way... \r\nBut since these are “state” APIs and one intended use case was that pages push/replace state URLs in a bflist that could actually be restored at a later date, we didn’t see the harm in also scripting a useful title in those entries as the user might actually confront them later.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
