    "created_at": "2019-11-07T17:24:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-11-07T17:24:51Z",
    "body": "The thing is, the spec doesn't get to dictate what browsers do in their user interfaces. Browsers could very well use this argument to change the user interface label for the given browsing context if they wanted to. They can't change the value of `document.title`, which is derived from the `<title>` element, but they can update their UA using any hints they wish.\r\n\r\nThis is similar to how specs dictate the value of `document.URI`, but do not dictate what gets displayed in the address bar.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
